DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("5*(x/2)");
$fun_1 = Formula("7/((cos(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-9, 4, 7} U (-infinity, 14]) U (-infinity, 14]");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, 4, 7}) U (2, infinity)");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("((-infinity, 14]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 14]) U {-9, 4, 7} U (-infinity, 14]");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(((-infinity, 13]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {7, 8, 9})) U {7, 8, 9} U ((-infinity, 13] U {7, 8, 9})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("((-infinity, 13] - ({7, 8, 9} U ((-infinity, 13] U (-infinity, 13]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({7, 8, 9} U ({7, 8, 9})))))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("((-infinity, 13] - {7, 8, 9})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`14/14+1/19`]? [_____]{1.05263157895}
---

What is the value of [`16.88+2.36+6.07`]? [_____]{answer=>25.31,width=>4}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{7, 8, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 13\}`]

Compute:
- [`((B) \cap A) \cup A \cup (B \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B - (A \cup (B \cup B) \cap (A \cup (A))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 14\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 1\}`]
- [`C = \{-9, 4, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C \cup A) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cap C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`(A) \cap A \cup C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, -9, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -10, -1, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, -9, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, -1, 7>") x Compute("<-7, -9, 4>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, -1, 7>") . Compute("<-7, -9, 4>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-10, -1, 7>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-10, -1, 7>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, 0, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -8, -9, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -9, 8, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 0, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-8, -9, 2>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-9, 8, -5>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-7, 0, 6>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
